7592186045417] [17592186379980 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379980 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $X$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(X)=10.$ What is the value of $det(6X)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379980 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "409f716a-c0ac-55a0-a174-94c6fcabcec4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379980 #edb/ref 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6X) & ={6}^{3}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =216\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =2160.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186379985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379981 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "37d4f007-41c0-5c4c-afc3-772d63dabd28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379982 #edb/ref 1080 "180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379982 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379982 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e82175b-bea8-5a74-b02e-c936593b97ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379983 #edb/ref 1080 "60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379983 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379983 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74d9c464-c1d9-5c1c-9898-e524d4a223c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379984 #ed