487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385571 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $Y$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(Y)=84.$ The matrix $Z$ is obtained from $Y$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{7}$ and ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.$ What is the value of $det(Z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385571 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7dd7b936-dcd4-5588-8ef8-d567f8396fba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385571 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{7}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\nTherefore, we only have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & =-det(Y) \\\\  & =-(84) \\\\  & =-84.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385572 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ee630750-cac3-50bd-8769-0e87a844e96e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385573 #edb/ref 1080 "-42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4dba8559-0132-5214-a523-39faf0ee84e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385574 #edb/ref 108