17592186409689 #edb/ref 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2Y) & ={2}^{6}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0f93ad19-15c5-55b8-98ea-d5bcee8f0a3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2aef95ee-e7e9-5cac-b9ad-3b67a53db79f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2df25dd7-50b3-560b-9abe-b6b13654a237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e6fad07-ec42-5416-85eb-9ef2b0059cbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409696 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409696 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d75809ee-199d-50e2-b002-2326810f1174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409696 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409689 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
